<!--
  The public marketing URLs (docs/redesign/seo-content-strategy.md §5).
  App, onboarding, admin and auth routes are deliberately absent: they are
  noindex, and three of the four are also disallowed in robots.txt.

  `lastmod` is omitted on purpose. The spec allows either a real per-page
  content-change date or nothing at all, and forbids a fake always-today
  value — an untrue lastmod on every URL teaches crawlers to ignore the
  signal. A real one needs the build to stamp dates from git history, which
  arrives with the prerender step.

  `priority` and `changefreq` are omitted: Google ignores both.
-->
